## Root Cause Analysis

**Issue**: WebSocket connection not closed on unmount. When navigating away, the WebSocket stays open and continues calling `setData` on an unmounted component, causing memory leak.

**Root Cause Category**: missing_cleanup

## Fix
```tsx
function Dashboard() {
  const [data, setData] = useState([]);

  useEffect(() => {
    const ws = new WebSocket('wss://api.example.com/live');

    ws.onmessage = (event) => {
      setData(prev => [...prev, JSON.parse(event.data)]);
    };

    ws.onerror = (error) => {
      console.error('WebSocket error:', error);
    };

    // Cleanup function
    return () => {
      ws.close();
    };
  }, []);

  return <Chart data={data} />;
}

// Also consider limiting data array size:
useEffect(() => {
  const ws = new WebSocket('wss://api.example.com/live');

  ws.onmessage = (event) => {
    setData(prev => {
      const newData = [...prev, JSON.parse(event.data)];
      // Keep only last 1000 items
      return newData.slice(-1000);
    });
  };

  return () => ws.close();
}, []);
```

## Verification
- WebSocket closes on unmount
- No "setState on unmounted component" warnings
- Memory usage stable over time
- Use React DevTools Profiler to detect leaks
